      <div type="clause" n="51">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 51</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="51" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>XCV. Gif gesiðcund<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.5-3"/> mon landagende forsitte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.6-3"/> fierd, g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>selle CXX scill. ⁊ ðolie his landes; unlandagende LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.7-2"/> scill.; cierlisc XXX scill. to<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.8-2"/> fierdwite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="51" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>XCV. Gif gesiðcund mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.4-2"/> londagende<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.5-2"/> fyrd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.6-2"/> forsitte, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.7"/> CXX scll' ⁊ þolige his londes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.5-2"/>; <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.8"/>londagende<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.5-2"/> LX scillinga; ceorlisc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.9"/> XXX to fyrdwite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="51" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe gesiðcund man fyrde forsitte. Gyf se siðcunde man landagende fyrde forsitte, gesylle hundtwelftig scill' ⁊ ðolie his landes; unlandagende syxti scill'; ceorlisc ðrittig scill' to wite.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="51" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="113" ed="#liebermann"/>Si homo siþcundus terram<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.2"/> habens (terrarius) fird<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.3"/> (expeditionem) supersedeat, emendet C uiginti sol. et perdat terram suam; non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.4"/> habens terram LX sol.; cyrliscus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.5"/> XXX solid. pro fyrdwita.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_51.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="52" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be þam þe gesiðcund man fyrde forsitte.] Gif gesiðcund<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_51.attnote.fn.13"/> mon landagende forsitte fierd<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#Ine_51.attnote.fn.14"/>, geselle CXX scill. ⁊ ðolie his landes; unlandagende LX scill.; cierlisc XXX scill. to fierdwite<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Ine_51.attnote.fn.15"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="54" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="414" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XCV} Gif gesiðcund mon landagende forsitte fierd, <hi rend="italic">ge</hi>selle CXX sciƚƚ ⁊ ðolie his landes; unlandagende LX sciƚƚ; cierlisc XXX sciƚƚ to fierdwite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="113" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Mann vom Gefolgsadel, ein Grundbesitzer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_51.lnote.de.1"/>, die Heerfahrt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_51.lnote.de.2"/> versitzt, zahle er 120 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_51.lnote.de.3"/> und verliere sein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_51.lnote.de.4"/> Land [an den Verleiher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_51.lnote.de.5"/>]; ein [Gefolgsmann] ohne Grundeigenthum 60<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_51.lnote.de.6"/> Schill.; ein gemeinfreier [Mann] 30 Schill.: als Heer[versäumniss]-Strafe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a man of the retainer nobility, a landholder, neglects military service, let him pay 120 shillings and lose his land [to the grantor]; a [retainer] without landed property, 60 shillings; a common [freeman], 30 shillings: as the fine for [neglecting] military service.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="53" ed="#attenborough"/>If a nobleman who holds land neglects military service<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_51.attnote.n.1"/>, he shall pay 120 shillings and forfeit his land; a nobleman who holds no land shall pay 60 shillings; a commoner shall pay a fine of 30 shillings for neglecting military service.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="405" ed="#whitelock"/>If a <hi rend="italic">gesith-born</hi> man, who owns land, neglects military service, he is to give 120 shillings and to forfeit his land; one who owns no land, 60 shillings, a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> 30 shillings, as fine for [neglect of] military service.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="415" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a nobly born man who owns property neglects [his duty to serve] in the army, let him pay 120 shillings and forfeit his land; [a noble] who does not own property, 60 shillings; a man of ceorl-wer, 30 shillings as fyrd-fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="344"><ref target="clause:VAtr_26-1">V Atr 26.1–30</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geänd. in</hi> ferdwite</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to ferdwite in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> t. h. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> terrarius <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only t. h. Lond; only terrarius the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur Co am Rande:</hi> fird id est expedicio; <hi rend="italic">fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only Co, in the margin: fird id est expedicio; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">non h. t. <hi rend="italic">überspringt M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">non h. t. omitted by M</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cirl. <hi rend="italic">Lond T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cirl. Lond T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> fir. <hi rend="italic">R T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy. K; fir. R T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> mann</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to mann</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> fyrde</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to fyrde</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">davor fehlt</hi> un</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">un is missing before it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">se siþcundman <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">se siþcundman Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fyrde for., gesylle hundtwelftig sc. ⁊ þolige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fyrde for., gesylle hundtwelftig sc. ⁊ þolige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig sc., ceorlisc ðrittig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig sc., ceorlisc ðrittig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">to f. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to f. lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Earle meint (<hi rend="italic">Landchar.</hi> xxx) grundlos, dass hier <hi rend="italic">land</hi> nur <hi rend="italic">eðel</hi> und <hi rend="italic">bocland,</hi> nicht auch <hi rend="italic">folcland</hi> bedeute</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Earle (<hi rend="italic">Landchar.</hi> xxx) thinks without good reason that <hi rend="italic">land</hi> here means only <hi rend="italic">eðel</hi> and <hi rend="italic">bocland,</hi> not also <hi rend="italic">folcland</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Gefolgsadel 11. 14; Heer 2. 8a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Gefolgsadel 11. 14; Heer 2. 8a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">D. i. Königs ‘Ungehorsam’; <hi rend="italic">s. d.</hi> 8. Die Heerversäumnis ward später weit höher gestraft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">I.e. the king’s ‘disobedience’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 8. Neglect of military service was later punished far more heavily</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Coenwulf von Mercien verleiht Land <hi rend="italic">ministro in sempiternam possessionem, si nobis et optimatibus nostris manserit minister et inconvulsus amicus;</hi> a. 801 Bi 303</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Coenwulf of Mercia grants land <hi rend="italic">ministro in sempiternam possessionem, si nobis et optimatibus nostris manserit minister et inconvulsus amicus;</hi> a. 801 Bi 303</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> læn 3. 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> læn 3. 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_51.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">77</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Strafe (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 11) in Geld steigt zwar allgemein mit höherem Stande; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13. Hier aber auch mit des Betroffenen besonderer Pflicht, das Bedrohte zu vermeiden: belehnter Gefolgsadel war in höherem Grade kriegspflichtig als unbelehnter oder Gemeinfreier. Das normale Strafgeldfixum (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5. 12. 13) wird gegen ihn verdoppelt, bzw. vervierfacht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The penalty (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 11) in money does indeed generally rise with higher rank; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13. Here, however, it rises also with the particular duty of the person concerned to avoid the act threatened with punishment: gesithcund nobility endowed with land was liable to military service to a higher degree than gesithcund nobility without land or the common freeman. The normal fixed fine (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5. 12. 13) is doubled, or quadrupled, against him</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_51.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>gesiðcund</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">se siðcunde</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">se siþcundman</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_51.attnote.fn.14" n="14" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>fierd</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">fyrde</hi>. B &amp; H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_51.attnote.fn.15" n="15" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">52</biblScope></bibl><label>fierdwite</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðrittig scill' to wite</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_51.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The original meaning of this word was ‘journey’ (cf. Norse <hi rend="italic">ferð</hi>), then (military) ‘expedition’; and in view of the fact that the Latin translation is nearly always <hi rend="italic">expeditio</hi>, it would possibly be better to translate the sentence, ‘if a nobleman etc. neglects to go on a (military) expedition.’ The custom arose, perhaps, not from state conscription but from the obligation of a dependant to accompany his lord on journeys (cf. reference to the <hi rend="italic">Eyrbyggja Saga</hi> given in note to cap. 33). I take <hi rend="italic">gesiðcund man landagende</hi> to be equivalent to <hi rend="italic">twelfhynde man</hi> (cf. cap. 45), and the <hi rend="italic">gesiðcund man unlandagende</hi> to be equivalent to <hi rend="italic">syxhynde man.</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
